Mexican Style Pork Chorizo
Makes 6 servings 
---------------------------------

Ingredients
-----------
1 lbs ground 80% lean pork
2 Tbsp smoked paprika
2 Tbsp paprika
1 Tbsp ancho chili powder
1 Tbsp chili powder
1/2 Tbsp ground cumin
1 tsp dried oregano
1 tsp ground coriander
1 tsp kosher salt
1/2 tsp ground cinnamon
2 Tbsp distilled white vinegar
2 cloves garlic, minced

Instructions
------------
- Mix together paprika, cumin, ancho chili powder, chili powder, oregano, coriander, salt, cinnamon, and cloves 
- Pour mixed chorizo seasoning over ground pork, white vinegar, and garlic in a large bowl
- Mix together by hand until well combined
- Heat 2 Tbsp of olive oil in a large cast iron skillet over medium-high heat
- Add the chorizo and cook for 8 to 10 minutes stiring frequently with a spatula until browned
